    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1010">

                <pb facs="0764" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 703.3212/23.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Brazilian Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>265. Your September 29. The strain upon you has been so great that we appreciate
                    your need of a vacation and rest, and shall approve of your course in leaving
                    whenever you feel that you should go. We are glad, however, that you think it
                    wise and possible to remain until the present situation clears up. We shall be
                    pleased to follow your wishes in regard to a representative during your absence.
                    Matters might be left with your Chargé, who, as the head of your Legation, could
                    represent us, acting in conjunction with Silliman or some other American as an
                    adviser.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
